> I started a new healer last night, and dove down to the mine shops.  I 
> made it to the temple with 2400 AU while still lvl 1!  It was a near 
> thing:  a wand of striking knocked me down to 1 HP, but I zapped the 
> holder with a wand of sleep and my dog finished him off.  Phew!  I'm 
> quite proud to have accomplished that on my first try.

Well done.

> Question:  I had a choice between +3 dwarven mithril and +0 studded 
> leather.  I chose the leather, so I could still cast spells with a 
> reasonable chance of success.  Was this wrong?  The -9 AC with the 
> mithril seemed awfully nice (-4 with the leather).

The mithril for sure.  You don't have the spells, mana, and mana regen at 
this point to make it worthwhile. 

> Question:  what weapon should I be using?  From reading some of your 
> suggestions, I think I'm really too much of a hand-to-hand fighter, 
> which doesn't make sense for a healer.  I have a composite bow, but it's 
> hard to find arrows.  Right now, I'm just killing things with my 
> scalpel.  :P

The scalpel is horrid :(  I recommend wielding a dagger and throwing daggers 
and darts.  As you increase your skill in those weapons, you will sometimes 
throw multiples per turn.

Untap traps to get more darts.
 
> Question:  is it my imagination, or can you safely throw a cursed 
> dagger?  Shouldn't it stick to your hand?

> Spellbooks:  healing, extra healing, stone to flesh

Extra healing is pretty good in combat, until you run out of mana...

Ideally you would have a robe so you could wear the mithril and still have a 
reasonable fail rate in extra healing.

